# Reproducible API + download caches
data/cache/

# Private / enterprise artifacts — SECOND layer only. The primary boundary is
# enforced in code at serialization time (src/boundary.py strips private
# values from public snapshots; export_private_snapshot writes only under
# EROOM_PRIVATE_ROOT, which must be OUTSIDE this repo). These patterns are a
# backstop so a stray private write can't be `git add`-ed by accident. They
# are NOT the boundary — never rely on them alone. See BOUNDARY.md.
data/private/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.npz

# Regenerable graph snapshots — ALL of data/exports/ is untracked (2026-06-30
# boundary/hygiene decision). Snapshots are large (10s–100s of MB) and rebuildable
# via scripts/build_graph.py (... --assemble). Per the public/private boundary
# (docs/dev/reports/BOUNDARY.md): any *sellable* snapshot (carrying private beliefs)
# lives in eroom-enterprise, and any public demo snapshot is distributed via a
# GitHub Release / artifact store — never committed in-tree. Paid inputs
# (data/annotations/, data/corpora/) stay tracked. This also prevents a future
# `git add -A` sweeping in bloat (the 2.5 GB blob incident). See CLEANUP_MERGE_REPORT.md.
data/exports/*.json

# Regenerable working artifacts: dev scratch outputs + HTML graph visualizations.
data/dev/
data/viz/

# Local scratch / out-of-baseline notes
onboarding/

# Per-round audit notes, design docs, inspection snapshots, and the
# automated debug-loop playbook. Local-only — these are the operator's
# working notes rather than published artifacts.
audit/
automate_node_debug.md
NEXT_SESSION.md

# Internal strategy / methodology docs — kept private (the repo is public, but
# the public/private boundary spec, the ML-vs-graph benchmark, the scaling plan,
# the hyperparameter registry, and the trust ledger are operator-internal, not
# published artifacts). NOTE: CLAUDE.md is intentionally KEPT (a generic
# contributor/agent orientation doc); detailed evolving state lives in private
# Claude memory, not in-repo.
BOUNDARY.md
BENCHMARK.md
SCALING.md
HYPERPARAMETERS.md
TRUST_LEDGER.md
# Strategic/methodology docs moved to the private eroom-enterprise repo
# (eroom-enterprise/docs/) and untracked here — kept out of the open-core repo.
BOUNDARY_SPLIT_PLAN.md
MERGE_PLAN.md
CLEANUP_MERGE_REPORT.md
ROUND23_ASSESSMENT.md
B1_BUILD_RESULTS.md
B1_DECISION.md
B1_DESCRIPTOR_AUDIT.md
SAFETY_MANIFOLD_ALIGNMENT.md
SAFETY_MANIFOLD_RESULTS.md
eroom-architecture-v2.md
eroom-em-derivation.md
current_tasks_graphfix.md
# Belt-and-suspenders: the operator's license/moat note is a Claude *memory* file
# that lives OUTSIDE the repo; ignore the name in case a copy ever lands in-tree.
project_license.md

# Operator-internal md reports — PERMANENT. ALL generated experiment/result/audit
# markdown (CLEANUP_RESULTS, *_RESULTS, REPO_AS_BUILT, etc.) lives here and is
# NEVER tracked. Do not remove this entry; do not commit anything under it. New
# experiment write-ups go in docs/dev/reports/, not the repo root.
docs/dev/reports/
